{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1a10dde4-4cbc-49d7-905e-ae04821998b5","session_id":"a3b4c75a-9a3d-40f5-97da-343064f2660c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1a10dde4-4cbc-49d7-905e-ae04821998b5","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL. Here's a summary of all changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### Fix 1: `Logbook.java` — `tripExists` excludes current trip during edit\n\n**Problem:** `tripExists(Trip trip)` checks all trips in the DB for date overlap but doesn't exclude the trip being edited. When a user edits a trip's dates, the original DB record always overlaps with itself, causing a false \"trip already exists\" error.\n\n**Fix:** Added an overloaded `tripExists(Trip trip, UUID excludeId)` method that skips the trip with the given ID.\n\n### Fix 2: `ManageTripFragment.java` — Pass editing ID to `tripExists`\n\n**Problem:** The validation call didn't pass the editing trip's ID.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `Logbook.tripExists(getNewTrip())` to `Logbook.tripExists(getNewTrip(), isEditing() ? getEditingId() : null)`.\n\n### Fix 3: `TripCursor.java` — Read `notes` from correct column\n\n**Problem:** `TripCursor.getTrip()` read the `notes` field from `CatchTable.Columns.NOTES` instead of `TripTable.Columns.NOTES` — a typo that would corrupt trip notes data when loading from the database.\n\n**Fix:** Removed the incorrect `CatchTable` import and changed `getColumnIndex(CatchTable.Columns.NOTES)` to `getColumnIndex(TripTable.Columns.NOTES)`."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59119,"output_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":56592,"total_tokens":59434}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"08f182a6-c50a-44d8-8e1c-11badfc8a048","session_id":"a3b4c75a-9a3d-40f5-97da-343064f2660c","is_error":false,"duration_ms":113305,"duration_api_ms":71735,"num_turns":23,"result":"\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL. Here's a summary of all changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### Fix 1: `Logbook.java` — `tripExists` excludes current trip during edit\n\n**Problem:** `tripExists(Trip trip)` checks all trips in the DB for date overlap but doesn't exclude the trip being edited. When a user edits a trip's dates, the original DB record always overlaps with itself, causing a false \"trip already exists\" error.\n\n**Fix:** Added an overloaded `tripExists(Trip trip, UUID excludeId)` method that skips the trip with the given ID.\n\n### Fix 2: `ManageTripFragment.java` — Pass editing ID to `tripExists`\n\n**Problem:** The validation call didn't pass the editing trip's ID.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `Logbook.tripExists(getNewTrip())` to `Logbook.tripExists(getNewTrip(), isEditing() ? getEditingId() : null)`.\n\n### Fix 3: `TripCursor.java` — Read `notes` from correct column\n\n**Problem:** `TripCursor.getTrip()` read the `notes` field from `CatchTable.Columns.NOTES` instead of `TripTable.Columns.NOTES` — a typo that would corrupt trip notes data when loading from the database.\n\n**Fix:** Removed the incorrect `CatchTable` import and changed `getColumnIndex(CatchTable.Columns.NOTES)` to `getColumnIndex(TripTable.Columns.NOTES)`.","usage":{"input_tokens":1866028,"output_tokens":23284,"cache_read_input_tokens":1556960,"total_tokens":1889312},"permission_denials":[]}
